claim.claim-text:
- in an unloaded condition, i.e. when there is no or only a limited axial load on the tubulars, only a limited number of windings, i.e. for the tubular windings located near the end of the tubular and for the coupling sleeve windings located away of the end of the coupling sleeve, is in engagement;
- during an increase in axial load on the riser section, the tubulars, and in particular the section of the tubular comprising the screw thread, elongates, and an increasing number of windings of the tubulars come into engagement with the windings of the coupling sleeve; and
- in a fully loaded condition, i.e. when there is a significant axial load on the tubulars e.g. by the riser section supporting a riser hanging in a bore hole, all windings, i.e. for the tubular also the windings located away from the end of the tubular and for the coupling sleeve also the windings located near the end of the coupling sleeve, are in engagement.
